"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"Celeste 64 is an Archipelago core game, meaning it does not require a custom world file (.apworld).\nBecause of this, aside from installing the mods, all you need to do is create your YAML file using the 'Options Creator' in the AP Launcher and send it to the person hosting the AP multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is setup, go to the 'Celeste64 Archipelago' folder in your 'Documents' directory (you can find it directly by clicking the folder icon on the setup tab) and open 'AP.json'.\n\nIn the 'Url' field, enter archipelago.gg: followed by the port. This is a 5-digit number that you can find on the website after creating a new room.\n\nIn 'SlotName', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nThe 'Password' field is optional. If the host didn't set one, simply leave it blank.\n\nFinally, go back to the 'Celeste64 Archipelago' folder and launch 'Celeste64.exe' and you can start playing!",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
